        <title type="html"><![CDATA[docs(webgl): clarify srcData allows null to allocate storage and fix uncompressed texture descriptions]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/46515</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/46515"/>
        <updated>2026-11-13T22:27:37.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/97598943?u=cd9a00667ac696f00f22df916bc5609963b33f4f&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/>
<p dir="auto"><span class="issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se" aria-label="This pull request closes issue #46493.">Closes</span> <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="6353819118" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/46493" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/46493/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/46493">#46493</a></p>
<h3 dir="auto">Summary of changes</h3>
<ol dir="auto">
<li><strong>Clarify <code class="notranslate">srcData: null</code> allocation</strong>:
<ul dir="auto">
<li>In <code class="notranslate">WebGLRenderingContext.texImage2D()</code> and <code class="notranslate">WebGL2RenderingContext.texImage3D()</code>, explicit mention is added that <code class="notranslate">srcData</code> may be <code class="notranslate">null</code> to allocate texture storage without uploading pixels. WebGL implementations initialize this allocated storage to zeros to prevent information leakage.</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li><strong>Correct uncompressed texture parameter descriptions</strong>:
<ul dir="auto">
<li>In <code class="notranslate">texImage2D</code>, <code class="notranslate">texSubImage2D</code>, <code class="notranslate">texImage3D</code>, and <code class="notranslate">texSubImage3D</code>, <code class="notranslate">srcData</code> was described as <em>"containing the compressed texture data"</em>. That wording was a copy-paste remnant from <code class="notranslate">compressedTexImage2D</code> / <code class="notranslate">compressedTexImage3D</code>. These methods handle uncompressed image/pixel data, so the description now accurately specifies <em>"containing the image pixel data"</em>.</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ol>
<h3 dir="auto">Verification</h3>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>Ran <code class="notranslate">npx prettier -c</code> on all 4 modified files (Passed).</li>
<li>Ran <code class="notranslate">npx markdownlint-cli2</code> on all 4 modified files (Passed — 0 issues).</li>
<li>Ran <code class="notranslate">npx cspell</code> on all 4 modified files (Passed — 0 issues).</li>
<li>Ran <code class="notranslate">npm test</code> (<code class="notranslate">node --test</code>) — all 27 tests across 4 suites passed (0 failures).</li>
</ul>]]></content>
