        <title type="html"><![CDATA[FF161 Clipboard API web custom formats: docs fixes]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/46506</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/46506"/>
        <updated>2026-11-13T05:33:09.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">FF161 enables support for Clipboard API web custom formats (MIME types prefixed with <code class="notranslate">web </code>) by default in <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2053725" rel="nofollow">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2053725</a></p>
<p dir="auto">Summary below, but mostly this is better cross-linking.</p>
<p dir="auto">This fixes some gaps in the custom formats docs:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li><code class="notranslate">ClipboardItem()</code>, <code class="notranslate">ClipboardItem</code>, <code class="notranslate">ClipboardItem.types</code>, <code class="notranslate">ClipboardItem.getType()</code> and <code class="notranslate">ClipboardItem.supports()</code> now mention and link to custom formats.</li>
<li><code class="notranslate">Clipboard.write()</code>: <code class="notranslate">NotAllowedError</code> also covers unsupported types, including a <code class="notranslate">web </code> type that isn't a correctly structured MIME type.</li>
<li>Clipboard API overview: security note that custom format data may have been written by another site or application.</li>
<li>Minor: a typo, and <code class="notranslate">reload(true)</code> → <code class="notranslate">reload()</code> in the examples.</li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="6311659002" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/46463" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/46463/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/46463">#46463</a></p>]]></content>
