<p dir="auto">Very small change to the language in the values for <code class="notranslate">stroke-width</code> to make it more clear. If I had to assume I think the original "see above" came from duplicating docs from similar pages like <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/stroke-dashoffset#values" rel="nofollow"><code class="notranslate">stroke-dashoffset</code></a> which orders it's values like <code class="notranslate">&lt;number&gt;</code>, <code class="notranslate">&lt;length&gt;</code> <code class="notranslate">&lt;percentage&gt;</code> which <em>would</em> mean number is "above"</p>

<h3 dir="auto">Motivation</h3>
<p dir="auto">Confusing to read as is, "see above where?"</p>]]></content>
