        <title type="html"><![CDATA[[Technical review] BiDi emulation module - `setGeolocationOverride` command]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/46498</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/46498"/>
        <updated>2026-11-13T19:06:15.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23019147?u=4c0de81596ced64dc067dea5686f7ca2912db0cb&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>
<p dir="auto">This PR adds the page for <code class="notranslate">emulation.setGeolocationOverride</code> command, with corresponding updates to the module overview page and the sidebar.</p>
<div class="markdown-alert markdown-alert-note" dir="auto"><p class="markdown-alert-title" dir="auto"><svg data-component="Octicon" class="octicon octicon-info mr-2" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M0 8a8 8 0 1 1 16 0A8 8 0 0 1 0 8Zm8-6.5a6.5 6.5 0 1 0 0 13 6.5 6.5 0 0 0 0-13ZM6.5 7.75A.75.75 0 0 1 7.25 7h1a.75.75 0 0 1 .75.75v2.75h.25a.75.75 0 0 1 0 1.5h-2a.75.75 0 0 1 0-1.5h.25v-2h-.25a.75.75 0 0 1-.75-.75ZM8 6a1 1 0 1 1 0-2 1 1 0 0 1 0 2Z"></path></svg>Note</p><p dir="auto">The <a href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/blob/2f32d3386b55a5486c698377ff372e6148a556d6/webdriver/bidi/emulation.json#L47">Firefox note in BCD</a> explicitly states that the global configuration is not yet supported.<br>
My testing in Chrome shows the same limitation: omitting both scope selectors returns <code class="notranslate">invalid argument</code>: “Either user contexts or browsing contexts must be provided”. However, there's no such note for Chrome in BCD.</p>
<p dir="auto">The current version of the page aligns with the spec to say that session-wide overrides are applied when neither <code class="notranslate">contexts</code> nor <code class="notranslate">userContexts</code> is specified. Let me know if this needs to be changed to the implemented behaviour instead.</p>
</div>
<h3 dir="auto">Spec link</h3>
<ul dir="auto">
<li><a href="https://w3c.github.io/webdriver-bidi/#command-emulation-setGeolocationOverride" rel="nofollow">https://w3c.github.io/webdriver-bidi/#command-emulation-setGeolocationOverride</a></li>
</ul>
